// Item 5 D: the chat Copilot's built jobs on recorded tool results (evals/sets/copilot_tools.json). Each case: the job it must route to, the tool calls in order, facts the answer must carry; with model_answer, whether a scripted model's wording is shown (ai) or the rules stay (rules). Jobs 3-5 (pre-trade check, position watch, post-trade coach) also check that their AI wording only describes (no instruction: the rules stay). Job 6 (the strategy builder) also checks the draft it hands over (expect_draft): PAPER, the values the trader's words state, every value they do not state left empty and asked for (never invented), "Not supported yet" for parts ATP cannot build, and no draft when nothing could be built. CP6-2 (the honest test of a complete draft on past data, `backtest_draft`) checks: the test runs only on his ask with every value his and a symbol named (else it says what is missing and calls no test), the facts (sample size, costs, drawdown, the earlier and later parts, the walk-forward windows, the luck-adjusted chance counted as one try), "too few trades" with no ratio judged, a failed read said plainly, the test offered as a follow-up (expect_followup) when not asked, and AI wording that promises or invents a number is not shown. Owner order 23 Oct ("its tools are wired"): job 1 adds market memory and the news feed, job 4 the news on the held symbols, job 9 (find setups: the trader's words as a screen, run on his own watchlist, explained, or an alert proposed for him to approve) and job 10 (the full view of a symbol: structure, option chain, news, market memory); a switched-off part is said plainly ("... is not set up yet"), never by its flag name.
